 ## Overview
-De-voxelization aggregates network predictions computed on a sparse set of unique voxels back to the original dense voxel grid, and subsequently reduces these per-voxel predictions into per-Gaussian predictions [S1, unofficial]. It serves as the inverse operation to 3D Gaussian Voxelization, enabling efficient processing by 3D networks that operate on voxelized representations while preserving the native Gaussian structure for final rendering [S1, unofficial].
