 ### Edge Cases and Pitfalls
-*   **Empty Gaussians**: If a Gaussian has zero voxels, `num_voxels_per_g` will contain a zero, causing duplicate values in the cumulative sum offset. The behavior of `segment_csr` on empty segments depends on the implementation; typically, it may return zeros or undefined values. Not given in the sources.
-*   **Index Bounds**: `inverse_indices` must contain valid indices within the range $[0, N_{\text{unique}})$. Out-of-bounds indices will cause errors [G].
-*   **Precision**: The choice of `REDUCE` mode affects precision. `"max"` and `"mean"` are the supported options [S1, unofficial].
